Sample Work
Retail Customer Intelligence — Online Retail II (518K transactions)
A UK-based online retailer needed to understand their customer base and identify revenue risks.
What I delivered:

Segmented 4,312 customers into 11 behavioral groups using RFM analysis
Identified that 6.7% of customers drive 50% of revenue — extreme concentration risk
Flagged 530 customers as churn risks, representing significant historical revenue
Forecasted weekly demand with seasonal modeling to support inventory planning
Provided specific recommendations per segment (loyalty programs for Champions, win-back campaigns for At Risk customers)

Fraud Detection — Credit Card Transactions (284K transactions)
A financial services team needed to identify fraudulent transactions in a dataset with a 0.17% fraud rate — 492 frauds hidden in 284,807 legitimate transactions.
What I delivered:

Built and compared 3 ML models, achieving 97%+ detection on the minority class
Identified the top predictive features driving fraud risk using SHAP explainability
Provided evaluation focused on precision and recall (not accuracy, which is meaningless at 99.8% class imbalance)
Documented the full modeling pipeline for reproducibility

Churn Prediction — Telco Customer Data (7,043 customers)
A telecom provider wanted to predict which customers would leave and understand the key drivers of churn.
What I delivered:

Predictive model identifying at-risk customers with 84% discriminative ability (ROC-AUC)
SHAP analysis revealing that contract type, tenure, and monthly charges are the top churn drivers
Specific business recommendations: incentivize annual contracts, implement 90-day onboarding, audit pricing for high-charge customers
Honest assessment of model limitations with transparent methodology


How It Works
Step 1: You share your data with me (CSV, Excel, JSON, or database export). Any format works.
Step 2: I run it through my analysis pipeline, reviewing the results and adding context specific to your business situation.
Step 3: You receive professional HTML reports you can open in any browser — self-contained, no software needed. Each report includes an executive summary, visualizations with plain-English explanations, and actionable recommendations.
Step 4: Optional follow-up call to walk through findings and discuss next steps.

My Toolkit
I built a proprietary analysis platform (10,700+ lines of Python) that automates the technical heavy lifting — data cleaning, statistical analysis, forecasting, segmentation, and machine learning. This means I can deliver thorough analysis on fast timelines at competitive rates.
The platform includes:

Automated data cleaning with a 0-100 health score that grades data quality before and after
Domain-aware analysis that adapts to your industry (retail, finance, healthcare, HR, crime, fraud)
5 forecasting methods compared automatically (Linear, Moving Average, Holt-Winters, ARIMA, Prophet)
Customer segmentation with RFM scoring, Pareto analysis, and churn risk quantification
ML classification with 3 models compared, proper imbalance handling, and SHAP explainability
Executive summaries with auto-generated business insights in every report

Every chart includes a written explanation of what it shows and what it means for your business. No unexplained numbers. No jargon without context.

Technical Background
For teams that want the technical details:

Languages: Python (pandas, numpy, scikit-learn, statsmodels, XGBoost, SHAP, matplotlib)
Specializations: Exploratory analysis, time series forecasting, customer analytics (RFM), binary classification, model explainability
Data handling: Automated type detection, missing value imputation, outlier treatment, feature engineering (binning, interactions, skewness correction)
Evaluation: F1-Score, ROC-AUC, PR-AUC, MCC, MAPE, cross-validation — using the right metric for each problem type
Code quality: 10,700+ lines, thoroughly documented with decision-level comments explaining WHY every algorithm choice was made


